revious single centre door stood, so the town's entrance, apron and doorway clearance keep the ground they already held; the other is `kind: aperture`, which claims a hole and nothing else. No glazing, closure, interior, attic room, white paint or historic function is claimed by any of the three, and the white of the engraving's paper is not evidence of paint. WHAT THIS DOES NOT SETTLE. The source is retrospective 1831 context printed in 1881, not proof of the building as it stood on 1835-07-01; the camera on it remains unsolved and is not enrolled in data/reference_views/. The compound's overall width, the wing and sub-roof silhouettes, the roof junctions, the text-attested partial clapboarding and the building's finish and tone are all unchanged and still open. T-2374's image gate stays open. See L-cobweb-apertures-2374."
