-  "change_note": "THE SCENE-DATE STATE IS A BUILDING SITE, NOT A BUILDING, and the record exists to keep it that way: data/exclusions.json carries lake_house_finished specifically to stop the completed hotel appearing in 1835, and says that on the scene date this is 'a partial three-story brick shell'. What is built here is one storey of brick with no roof, standing on a plan of invented size, with the storey count reasoned from an eighteen-month build schedule and tagged conjectural. The finished house - three storeys and a basement, elegantly furnished, nearly $100,000, opened in the autumn of 1836 under Jacob Russel - is a later phase that this project does not yet need and must not build into 1835.",
